{"archetypes":[{"name":"repo-binding","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff threads REPO through many scripts and failures here can target the wrong GitHub issue or repo.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether explicit repository resolution and --repo forwarding is consistent across /design entry, pause/resume, publish, postplan, current-env, and GitHub comment helpers. Pay special attention to argv precedence over source-env, omitted REPO hub-default behavior, and validation grammar mismatches that could produce divergent repositories. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"publish-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The change alters publish, pause, clarify, recovery, and step-sentinel state transitions that are easy to desynchronize.","prompt_body":"Trace the state machine around design-log-publish exit codes, PUBLISH_OK parsing, recovery branches, pause marker creation, clarify outcomes, and Step 5c completion sentinels. Look for paths where a contradictory envelope, missing envelope, failed publish, or empty SESSION_ID advances the workflow incorrectly or loses recovery metadata. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"summary-renderer","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds publish-skipped and failed-publish rendering semantics across primary and fallback summaries.","prompt_body":"Review the run-summary and final-summary rendering changes for outcome classification, Run logs path synthesis, primary versus degraded fallback parity, and design versus implement callsite compatibility. Check whether publish-skipped and failed-publish produce honest user-facing summaries without fake log paths or inappropriate recovery prose. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Several Bash helpers now parse untrusted env files and repo strings instead of sourcing or trusting them directly.","prompt_body":"Inspect the Bash boundary handling for untrusted source-env data, repo strings, command arguments, and stdout KEY=value parsing. Focus on quoting, set -e interactions, awk extraction behavior, newline/backslash/path traversal rejection, and whether any untrusted value can reach gh, file paths, or state files unsafely. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
